<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="<%= admin_locale %>">
  <head>
    <title><%= content_for(:title) || t("admin.layout.title") %></title>
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
    <%= csrf_meta_tags %>
    <%= csp_meta_tag %>
    <%= render "shared/theme_head" %>
    <%# Says on <html>, before anything is painted, whether this browser
        left the notes drawer open (`admin/shared/_notes_head`). %>
    <%= render "admin/shared/notes_head" %>
    <%= stylesheet_link_tag "tailwind", "data-turbo-track": "reload" %>
    <%= javascript_importmap_tags "admin" %>
    <%# Per-screen head tags: `turbo-cache-control: no-cache` on the API
        token reveal (admin/api_tokens/create), on the page and post
        editors (admin/pages/show, admin/posts/show) and on every screen with
        an explicit-save form (`Admin::SaveBarHelper#save_bar_form_data`). %>
    <%= yield :head %>
  </head>

  <%# CS Studio's shell (cs-studio spec §4.2, design pass spec §4): a grid of
      up to three columns -- modules, an optional page tree, and the main
      content frame -- plus, below 1280px, a top bar. The grid quietly
      collapses to two columns on any screen with no tree column of its own
      (every one but Pages -- `content_for :tree` is never set outside it).

      The sidebar and tree columns are *drawers* below 1280px / 1024px
      (`.admin-shell` in content-spiel.tailwind.css, handoff §9 A7): the same
      elements, slid off-screen until the top bar's buttons set `data-open`
      (`admin--drawer`, which also owns the scrim and Escape). That is real
      CSS rather than utilities because the open state is an attribute
      selector. `admin--drawer` joins `admin--dialog` on <body> -- both
      listen at the document level, and the existing dialog actions stay.

      `admin--notes` is on <body> for the same reason as `admin--dialog`: the
      editor header's Notes button, the markers on the block cards and the
      notes drawer are far apart in the document. The two drawer controllers
      tell each other when one opens (`admin--notes:opened`,
      `admin--drawer:opened`), so the notes drawer and a shell drawer are
      never open together -- but for the page tree folded beside the notes
      column, which is opened from it (`admin--notes#shellOpened`).

      `admin--notes-live` is the one thing in CS Studio that opens a socket
      (notes spec §6): on <body>, so every screen has the person's stream --
      the sidebar's count, the toast -- and so the parts that show one
      record's notes (its `record` targets: an editor's drawer, the media
      panel's notes, the mind graph's card) are found wherever they are
      drawn. Its values are the addresses of the parts it fetches again when
      a signal says something changed -- the delivery's is the address of
      delivery 0, a placeholder the route accepts, whose last path segment
      the script replaces with the id it was told (no text is searched for,
      so no `ADMIN_PATH` can collide with it); `tag` writes this tab's id on
      its notes writes, and `shown`, `fresh` and `visible` tell it that a
      drawer was opened, that the notes frame was loaded by Turbo itself and
      that the document can be seen again.

      `admin--notes-alert` hears what that controller announces (one delivery,
      already read through the scoped endpoint) and, for a mention, lets one
      tab of this person chime and, with no tab of theirs in view, one raise
      a desktop notification (notes spec §6.4). Its values are the person's
      two settings as they were when this page was drawn -- a change on the
      account screen takes effect with the next page -- and the person's id,
      which only names the `BroadcastChannel` their tabs agree on.

      `data-admin-locale` carries the editing language onto <body> (rather
      than one data attribute per component) so any Stimulus controller can
      read it via `closest` without a server round trip.

      `data-messages` is the strings the shared scripts show (the leave
      dialog's sentence, the save status line, the toasts a drop raises,
      the pending-lock hint -- `Admin::MessagesHelper`,
      `app/javascript/i18n/messages.js`); a script that finds no nearer
      `data-messages` reads these. %>
  <body data-controller="admin--dialog admin--drawer admin--command-palette admin--fragment-links admin--file-drop-guard admin--notes admin--notes-live admin--notes-alert" data-admin--command-palette-url-value="<%= admin_jump_path(**admin_url_options) %>"
        data-admin--notes-live-unread-url-value="<%= admin_unread_notes_path %>" data-admin--notes-live-card-url-value="<%= admin_notes_card_path(**admin_url_options) %>"
        data-admin--notes-live-open-threads-url-value="<%= admin_open_note_threads_path(**admin_url_options) %>"
        data-admin--notes-live-delivery-url-value="<%= admin_note_delivery_path(0, **admin_url_options) %>"
        data-admin--notes-alert-sound-value="<%= Current.user&.notes_sound ? true : false %>" data-admin--notes-alert-desktop-value="<%= Current.user&.notes_desktop ? true : false %>"
        data-admin--notes-alert-person-value="<%= Current.user&.id %>"
        data-action="mousedown->admin--dialog#remember click->admin--dialog#backdrop keydown.esc@window->admin--drawer#closeAll turbo:before-visit@document->admin--drawer#visiting turbo:frame-load@document->admin--drawer#frameLoaded selectionchange@document->admin--notes#selected mousedown->admin--notes#release:capture admin--notes:opened->admin--drawer#standAside admin--drawer:opened->admin--notes#shellOpened turbo:before-fetch-request@document->admin--notes-live#tag admin--notes:opened->admin--notes-live#shown turbo:frame-load@document->admin--notes-live#fresh visibilitychange@document->admin--notes-live#visible admin--notes-live:delivery@document->admin--notes-alert#delivery"
        data-admin-locale="<%= admin_locale %>" data-messages="<%= admin_script_messages %>" class="min-h-screen bg-paper font-cs text-ink scheme-light dark:scheme-dark">
    <%= render Admin::Shell::TopBarComponent.new(tree: content_for?(:tree)) %>
    <div class="admin-shell<%= " admin-shell--tree" if content_for?(:tree) %>">
      <%# `Admin::BaseController::MODULES`, narrowed to what this user can
          open (`admin_modules`, access-control design spec §5: sidebar
          modules are shown only when `can?`) -- a module they lack is
          simply absent, not greyed out; opening its URL anyway gets the
          403 page. `admin_url_options` is threaded through by the component
          (see its comment). `badges` are the counts beside two entries, keyed
          by the entry's path helper: the viewer's unread notes on Dashboard
          (one COUNT, `notes_badge_count`) and what they could act on in
          Trash. %>
      <div id="sidebar" class="admin-shell__sidebar" data-admin--drawer-target="panel" data-drawer="sidebar" tabindex="-1">
        <%= render Admin::Shell::SidebarComponent.new(modules: admin_modules, user: Current.user, current_path: request.path,
              url_options: admin_url_options, badges: { admin_root_path: notes_badge_count, admin_trash_path: trash_badge_count }) %>
      </div>

      <% if content_for?(:tree) %>
        <aside id="tree-column" class="admin-shell__tree" data-admin--drawer-target="panel" data-drawer="tree" tabindex="-1">
          <%= yield :tree %>
        </aside>
      <% end %>

      <%# `p-6` stays on <main>: the save bar (`sticky bottom-0 -mx-6`) is
          sized against it. %>
      <main class="admin-shell__main min-w-0 p-6">
        <turbo-frame id="content" data-turbo-action="advance">
          <%# A frame request's response keeps only this frame, so the flash
              it carries is rendered here (as bare toasts that `admin--toast`
              moves into `#toasts`) instead of in the region below, where it
              would be consumed and dropped. %>
          <%= render Admin::ToastRegionComponent.new(flash: flash, relay: true) if turbo_frame_request? %>
          <%= yield %>
        </turbo-frame>
      </main>
    </div>

    <div class="admin-shell__scrim" data-action="click->admin--drawer#closeAll" data-admin--drawer-target="scrim" hidden></div>

    <%# The one toast region (handoff §10): outside `#content` so a frame
        navigation never wipes it, and a Turbo Stream's `toast_stream` has a
        fixed target. Empty on a frame request -- see the relay above. %>
    <%= render Admin::ToastRegionComponent.new(flash: turbo_frame_request? ? {} : flash) %>

    <%# The error toast a drop clones when its request got no answer the
        server could have put a toast into -- offline, signed out, an error
        page (`autosave/order_request.js`, which writes the message in). The
        component's own markup, so such a toast is the same toast; inert and
        outside `#toasts` while it is a `<template>`. %>
    <template id="toast-error-template"><%= render Admin::ToastComponent.new(message: t("admin.components.toast.save_failed"), kind: :error) %></template>

    <%# The toast a note addressed to the viewer raises (notes spec §6.4; handoff
        "Toast"): the existing inverted toast with the action "Open", 8 seconds
        like Undo. `admin--notes-live` clones it and writes in the sentence,
        the accent dot and where "Open" leads; inert here, like the template
        above. "Open" is a GET, the one toast action that is: it opens a
        record's notes and writes nothing. %>
    <template id="toast-note-template"><%= render Admin::ToastComponent.new(message: t("admin.notes.script.toast.placeholder"), kind: :undo,
          action: { label: t("admin.notes.script.toast.open"), url: admin_notes_path, method: :get }) %></template>

    <%# The pending-suggestion box `admin--translate` clones into a field's
        suggestion slot before each AI request (`Admin::TranslationScreen::
        PendingComponent`): a `<template>` is inert, so its buttons and spinner
        do nothing here, and it sits outside every form. %>
    <template id="translation-pending-template"><%= render Admin::TranslationScreen::PendingComponent.new %></template>

    <%# The one Leave dialog (design pass spec §4; round 3 decision D24):
        `admin--save-bar` opens it when a Turbo visit, a link into the content
        frame or Back / Forward would drop unsaved changes. Here, outside
        `#content` and every form, like every dialog.
        "Keep editing" is the primary button and holds the initial focus, so
        Enter by reflex keeps the text; it is a plain `method="dialog"` submit
        (as are Escape, the × and a click on the backdrop) -- closing is all
        it does, because the guard stopped the way out before anything had
        started. "Discard changes" (`data-leave-confirm`) is wired per open,
        as a listener rather than an inline handler; its label alone is red,
        the dialog's one destructive choice without competing with the
        primary. The sentence is written by the controller as it opens the
        dialog ("You have 3 unsaved changes on this screen."); what is
        rendered here is the form without a number. %>
    <%= render Admin::DialogComponent.new(id: "leave-dialog", title: t("admin.layout.leave_dialog.title"), width: :confirm) do |dialog| %>
      <p class="text-ink" data-leave-count><%= t("admin.layout.leave_dialog.body") %></p>
      <% dialog.with_footer do %>
        <%= render Admin::ButtonComponent.new(label: t("admin.layout.leave_dialog.discard"), variant: :danger_text, type: "button", data: { leave_confirm: true }) %>
        <%= tag.form method: "dialog" do %>
          <%= render Admin::ButtonComponent.new(label: t("admin.layout.leave_dialog.keep_editing"), variant: :primary, type: "submit", autofocus: true) %>
        <% end %>
      <% end %>
    <% end %>

    <%# The one ⌘K palette (design pass spec §5.6): here, outside `#content`
        and every form, like every dialog. Opened by `admin--command-palette`
        on <body>, which also owns the ⌘K / Ctrl+K shortcut. %>
    <%= render Admin::Shell::CommandPaletteComponent.new %>

    <%# The one media picker (media library Task 8) -- here, outside the
        `#content` frame and every form, so there's exactly one per page
        however many image fields and editors open it, and its own inputs
        never feed an autosave. Renders nothing without `media.upload`
        (`Media::PickerComponent`'s own comment). %>
    <%= render Media::PickerComponent.new(url_options: admin_url_options) %>

    <%# The New page and New post dialogs (design pass round 2, Task 15): once
        each, here, outside `#content` and every form. Every "+ New page" /
        "New post" trigger (tree header and rows, ⌘K, the pages empty state,
        the dashboard, the posts list) opens one of these. Only the SHELL is
        rendered (no query, only for a viewer who holds the create right
        somewhere): the form loads into its turbo-frame when the dialog opens. The no-JS `new` pages render
        the same form on their own and skip the dialogs (`:standalone_new_record`),
        so no id appears twice. %>
    <% unless content_for?(:standalone_new_record) %>
      <%= render Admin::EditorScreen::NewPageDialogComponent.new(url_options: admin_url_options) %>
      <%= render Admin::EditorScreen::NewPostDialogComponent.new(url_options: admin_url_options) %>
    <% end %>

    <%# The rich-text editor's image, YouTube and Page link dialogs (design pass
        round 2, Task 13): one of each, here for the same reason as the picker
        -- outside `#content` and every autosave form. The editor that opens
        one is the only one that hears its answer. %>
    <%= render Admin::EditorScreen::RichTextDialogsComponent.new %>

    <%# The one form every "Still correct — mark up to date" button submits
        (`Admin::EditorScreen::ReferenceCardComponent`): empty, here
        outside `#content` and every autosave form for the same reason as
        the picker -- forms can't nest, so each button names this one as
        its owner (`form=`) and its own record in `formaction`. It carries
        only the CSRF token. %>
    <%= form_with url: admin_translation_confirmation_path, method: :post,
          id: Admin::EditorScreen::ReferenceCardComponent::FORM_ID, class: "hidden" do %>
    <% end %>
  </body>
</html>
